-- The protective statutes' root (MMS-601): the statutes that set a floor an
-- agreement, a circular and the takanon cannot go below — the Minimum Wage
-- Law, the Wage Protection Law, the Severance Pay Law, the Women's Work
-- Law, the Equal Opportunities Law, the Sick Pay Law with the four laws
-- of absence for a family member's illness or a partner's pregnancy that
-- charge to its accrued days, and the Annual Leave Law (l4/laws/*.l4) —
-- and the floor each sets for an item of the shared vocabulary
-- (l4/lib/vocabulary.l4), for a case.
-- It is a `collection root` (l4/lib/precedence.l4), but not one of the
-- collections the root sets against each other: its ruling is weighed
-- last, over whichever instrument their precedence left governing, by the
-- Collective Agreements Law's §21 (`the ruling under the statutes' floor`).
--
-- No item of the vocabulary is yet one of these statutes' floors: the
-- minimum wage is a floor on the pay its §3 counts, not on any one item,
-- severance and deductions are not monthly items, the Women's Work Law's
-- floors are leave, absences and limits on dismissal, and the Equal
-- Opportunities Law's is who has a right (a father, by §4), not how much,
-- the sick-pay laws' are days of absence and a limit on dismissal, and the
-- Annual Leave Law's are days of leave, when they are given, and their pay.
-- So this root's claims are empty for every item, and the floors are
-- weighed in the instruments' own files (the September 2016 agreement's
-- top-up, the 2023 framework's hourly floor, circular תשע"ג/10's
-- reduction, the completion agreement's §93, the takanon's §§1.25.5,
-- 1.28.2.1 and 1.28.2.3, the day-care and mother's-position instruments
-- against §4, the takanon's §1.25.3.1 against the sick-pay laws, its
-- §§1.25.1-1.25.2, 1.30, 2.1, 8.1 and 14 and the wage agreement of
-- 19.10.2022 against the Annual Leave Law); a new item a statute floors is
-- a new branch of `the statutes' claims on`, and the statute's module
-- (l4/laws/) is imported here then — not before, since the root, and the
-- calculator that ships everything it reaches, would load it for nothing.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT precedence

§ `שורש החוקים המגינים — הרצפה שחוק קובע`

§§ `המסמכים`

-- Each statute as an instrument. A statute is `a provision of law`, which
-- the takanon's introduction lets prevail whatever its date, and which §21
-- puts above every agreement; so its date is never weighed, and the day
-- here is the first of its year (the day of its passing is not pinned).
`the Minimum Wage Law` MEANS
    `instrument` WITH
        `module`        IS "minimum-wage-law"
        `title`         IS "חוק שכר מינימום, התשמ\"ז-1987"
        `kind`          IS `a provision of law`
        `is the takanon` IS FALSE
        `issued`        IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1987
        `practised for all state employees` IS TRUE
        `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS FALSE

`the Wage Protection Law` MEANS
    `instrument` WITH
        `module`        IS "wage-protection-law"
        `title`         IS "חוק הגנת השכר, התשי\"ח-1958"
        `kind`          IS `a provision of law`
        `is the takanon` IS FALSE
        `issued`        IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1958
        `practised for all state employees` IS TRUE
        `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS FALSE

